WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.173
Allow 4 minutes.

00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:04.123
A verb alone can conceal the thinking required.

00:00:04.363 --> 00:00:13.600
“Identify” might mean recognizing a memorized definition or separating relevant evidence from irrelevant details in an unfamiliar case.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:20.837
Read the content, conditions, reference materials, novelty, and required reasoning before assigning a category.

00:00:21.527 --> 00:00:31.042
Worked example: fictional rule card: tickets blocking the entire team’s login are urgent; a single user’s cosmetic display problem is routine.

00:00:31.282 --> 00:00:34.610
Selecting priority by executing this rule is Apply.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:41.250
Examining several incident reports to distinguish shared causes from isolated symptoms is Analyze.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:47.634
Judging two escalation proposals against response-time and capacity criteria is Evaluate.

00:00:47.874 --> 00:00:52.205
Developing a new triage plan with its own coherent workflow is Create.

00:00:52.895 --> 00:00:54.175
Knowledge matters too.

00:00:54.415 --> 00:00:56.783
The exact queue name is factual knowledge.

00:00:57.023 --> 00:01:00.585
The relationship between impact and urgency is conceptual.

00:01:00.825 --> 00:01:03.044
How to perform triage is procedural.

00:01:03.284 --> 00:01:10.708
Recognizing that your own confidence is low and choosing an appropriate checking strategy involves metacognitive knowledge.

00:01:10.948 --> 00:01:15.492
These dimensions describe the task, not the intelligence or worth of the learner.

00:01:16.182 --> 00:01:24.830
Thirty-second check: choose a familiar task and finish “The learner must use ___ knowledge to ___.” If unsure about the category, write the actual evidence

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.638
you would need to observe before choosing a label.

00:01:28.328 --> 00:01:29.416
Now it's your turn.

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:35.011
A quiz says “Analyze this term” but asks learners to select its memorized definition.

00:01:35.251 --> 00:01:36.467
How should you review it?

00:01:36.707 --> 00:01:39.821
Pause the video and make your choice in the activity below.

